      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Four men led by Townsend North and James M. built a dam on the Cass River and founded Vassar on March 1, 1849.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofvassar.org/181/History-of-Vassar",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Vassar’s historic library, the Bullard Sanford Memorial Library, was funded by a local Friends group and opened in the early 20th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.vassarlibrary.org/history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Michigan Central Bay City Branch and the Port Huron & Northwestern rail lines crossed in Vassar, making it a key rail junction in the Thumb region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
